 r"I am writing to apply for the Forward-Deployed AI Product Associate position at Euphoric. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have built AI tools for people who are not engineers, designed ways to evaluate whether those tools are good enough, and worked directly with the clients who rely on them. I am particularly interested in this role because it combines all three.",

 r"What attracts me most to Euphoric is that it is applying AI to a large, overlooked category where the end result is better support for employees' health and financial wellbeing, and that the role sits between engineering, product and the client rather than behind a ticket queue. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I analyse merchant and operations data in SQL and Python and build KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. I also built an AI agent using Claude Code that automates repetitive steps of the analytics workflow, and it is now used by my own team and by adjacent teams. Building it meant understanding the existing process, deciding which steps the agent should own and which still needed a person, and supporting colleagues as they adopted it, which is close to the internal agentic workflows this role describes.",

 r"My closest experience to the AI side of the role is DS Digital Technology, where I worked as a Data Scientist Intern on a patient-facing medical AI engagement for a pharmaceutical client. I designed a 246-question benchmark and six-dimension safety rubric with red-line rules, working with the client's clinical experts, and the client adopted it as its acceptance standard. I built the Python pipeline that called six LLM APIs with retrieval and search augmentation and scored more than 2,400 responses with an LLM-as-judge framework, and a regex and LLM extraction pipeline that turned more than 4,800 free-text patient consultation threads into structured data. I presented the findings and priorities to the client's stakeholders. Designing evaluation frameworks and extracting reliable structure from messy documents are both central to what Euphoric's platform needs.",

 r"At Ipsos Strategy3 I structured more than 80 healthcare professional interviews into quantitative variables to understand customer needs, which taught me how to turn what users say into something a product team can act on. My MSc dissertation used 458,840 UK Biobank participants and is delivered as a deployed Streamlit application.",

